<.shell current={:private} theme={@theme}>
  <h1>Private</h1>
  <p class="lead">Contact details blurred until tapped.</p>

  <div class="demo max-w-sm">
    <dl>
      <dt>Email</dt>
      <dd>
        <.private id="private-demo-email">
          <.email id="private-demo-copy-email" email="alex.chen@example.com" />
        </.private>
      </dd>
      <dt>Phone</dt>
      <dd>
        <.private id="private-demo-phone">
          <.phone id="private-demo-phone-number" phone="604-555-0112" />
        </.private>
      </dd>
      <dt>Address</dt>
      <dd>
        <.private id="private-demo-address">
          <.copy_button
            text="112 Example Road"
            id="private-demo-copy-address"
            value="112 Example Road"
            label="Copy address"
          />
        </.private>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A member's email, phone, address, and emergency contact on a page a team admin opens often, such as the member sidebar. Screens get shared and projected at meetings, and read over shoulders.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A page someone opens to reach a person, such as a call-out list. A tap before every call slows them down. Never to hide details from someone who shouldn't see them: they're still in the page. Leave those out.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    A 5px blur. The first tap shows the details, even on an email link; the next tap opens Mail. The copy button copies while blurred. Each page load blurs them again. A keyboard focus inside shows them while it's there.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.private id="…"&gt;…&lt;/.private&gt;</code>
    blurs the <code>.private-text</code>
    inside it. A copy button's text is one, so it works around <a href={page_path(:email)}>email</a>, <a href={
      page_path(:phone)
    }>phone</a>, and <a href={page_path(:copy_button)}>copy button</a>
    with nothing to add. Wrap other text in <code>&lt;span class="private-text"&gt;</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
